In `async-openai` `0.42`, API clients and types are behind feature flags (only `rustls` is enabled by default), and chat types live under `async_openai::types::chat`.

### 1. Enable the `chat-completion` feature in [Cargo.toml](file:///home/derek/projects/ryz/Cargo.toml#L19)

Update line 19 to enable `chat-completion` (or `full`):

```toml
async-openai = { version = "0.42.0", features = ["chat-completion"] }
```

### 2. Import chat types from `types::chat` in [ai.rs](file:///home/derek/projects/ryz/src/core/ai.rs#L5-L12)

Change `types::{...}` to `types::chat::{...}`:

```rust
use async_openai::{
    Client,
    config::OpenAIConfig,
    types::chat::{
        ChatCompletionRequestSystemMessageArgs, ChatCompletionRequestUserMessageArgs,
        CreateChatCompletionRequestArgs,
    },
};
```

