The API call succeeded, but the proxy server (`https://ry953ga.abc-tunnel.us/v1`) returned a **Server-Sent Events (SSE) stream** (`data: {"object":"chat.completion.chunk", ...}`) instead of a single JSON response (`chat.completion`).

[`Chat::create`](file:///home/derek/.cargo/registry/src/index.crates.io-1949cf8c6b5b557f/async-openai-0.42.2/src/chat.rs#L42-L57) expects a single JSON object, so `serde_json` fails on `data: ...` at line 1, column 1.

### Option 1: Explicitly pass `.stream(false)` (try this first)

By default, `CreateChatCompletionRequestArgs` sets `stream` to `None` (omitting it from the JSON body), and some proxies default to streaming unless `"stream": false` is explicitly sent. Add `.stream(false)` in [`text`](file:///home/derek/projects/ryz/src/core/ai.rs#L23-L36):

```rust
    let request = CreateChatCompletionRequestArgs::default()
        .max_tokens(512u32)
        .model("free")
        .stream(false)
        .messages([
```

### Option 2: Use `create_stream` (if the proxy always streams)

If the proxy ignores `"stream": false` and always returns SSE chunks, use [`Chat::create_stream`](file:///home/derek/.cargo/registry/src/index.crates.io-1949cf8c6b5b557f/async-openai-0.42.2/src/chat.rs#L75-L92) and collect the `delta.content` chunks into a `String` (requires `futures = "0.3"` or `tokio-stream = "0.1"` in [Cargo.toml](file:///home/derek/projects/ryz/Cargo.toml#L7-L22)):

```rust
use futures::StreamExt; // or: use tokio_stream::StreamExt;

// ... inside `text`:
    let mut stream = client.chat().create_stream(request).await?;
    let mut llm_response = String::new();

    while let Some(res) = stream.next().await {
        let chunk = res?;
        for choice in chunk.choices {
            if let Some(content) = choice.delta.content {
                llm_response.push_str(&content);
            }
        }
    }

    if llm_response.is_empty() {
        return Err("Empty response".into());
    }

    Ok(llm_response)
```

